        "content": "<p>ColonelToad opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15235\">PR #15235</a> from <code>ColonelToad:docs/valtype-kind-limits</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>wasm_valtype_kind</code> aborts for <code>v128</code> and for reference types that<br>\n<code>wasm_valkind_t</code> cannot express. The documentation in <code>doc-wasm.h</code> mentioned<br>\nthe abort but never said what to use instead, which is what #15088 ran into.</p>\n<p>This documents <code>wasmtime_valtype_t</code> / <code>wasmtime_valtype_new</code> as the supported<br>\npath for those types in both <code>doc-wasm.h</code> and <code>wasmtime/types/val.h</code>. It also<br>\nfixes the abort messages, which previously said that support for <code>v128</code><br>\nwas not implemented. <code>v128</code> is implemented; it just cannot be represented<br>\nby <code>wasm_valkind_t</code>.</p>\n<p>I verified this by building the C API and running the reproducer from the<br>\nissue; it now prints guidance on which API to use before aborting.</p>\n<p>Closes #15088</p>\n</blockquote>",
